            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0227" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/1915: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr. William Phillips, Personal
                        Representative of President Roosevelt in India</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-14T21:00:00-04:00">April 14, 1943—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>199. Your 278, April 11. While I have no objection to your making the request
                    referred to in the first paragraph of your 257, April 2, 4 p.m., on a purely
                    personal basis, I believe it would be inopportune to adopt the suggestion in the
                    final paragraph of that telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
